0031:     """
0032:     Recolor each black or blue connected component with the color of the marker that borders it most.
0033: 
0034:     Input structure
0035:     - The grid contains black regions, blue line components, and isolated non-black/non-blue marker pixels.
0036:     - Marker pixels are controls; the black and blue cells are the regions to recolor.
0037:     Rule
0038:     - Label black and blue cells separately using 4-connectivity.
0039:     - For each labeled component, count side-adjacencies to every marker pixel.
0040:     - Recolor the component with the marker color having the largest shared side boundary; equal counts use row-major marker order.
0041:     - Leave the marker pixels unchanged.
0042:     Key insight
0043:     - The color assignment is local to each original-color component and is decided by shared edge contact with nearby markers.
0044:     """
